---
layout: base.njk
title: Home
---

<header class="site-header">
  <div class="header-top">
    <a href="/" class="site-title">Kamil Rybacki</a>
    <div class="social-links">
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kamil-andrzej-rybacki/" class="social-link" aria-label="LinkedIn">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M16 8a6 6 0 0 1 6 6v7h-4v-7a2 2 0 0 0-2-2 2 2 0 0 0-2 2v7h-4v-7a6 6 0 0 1 6-6z"/><rect width="4" height="12" x="2" y="9"/><circle cx="4" cy="4" r="2"/></svg>
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/kamilrybacki" class="social-link" aria-label="GitHub">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M15 22v-4a4.8 4.8 0 0 0-1-3.5c3 0 6-2 6-5.5.08-1.25-.27-2.48-1-3.5.28-1.15.28-2.35 0-3.5 0 0-1 0-3 1.5-2.64-.5-5.36-.5-8 0C6 2 5 2 5 2c-.3 1.15-.3 2.35 0 3.5A5.403 5.403 0 0 0 4 9c0 3.5 3 5.5 6 5.5-.39.49-.68 1.05-.85 1.65-.17.6-.22 1.23-.15 1.85v4"/><path d="M9 18c-4.51 2-5-2-7-2"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="site-description">
    <span class="dotted-line"></span>
    <p>Carving out a foothold in a shifting digital landscape</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="hero-section">
  <div class="hero-bg">
    <img src="/public/images/hero-dungeon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy">
    <div class="hero-gradient"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-content">
    <p>
      I'm a <strong>software developer</strong> with roots in <strong>Python backend engineering</strong>
      who's grown into designing systems at the architectural level — thinking about
      <strong>reusable patterns</strong>, sustainable codebases, and how to make software that holds up
      as requirements shift. 
    </p>
    <p>
      Lately, I've been drawn to the frontier of <strong>AI-augmented workflows</strong>:
      how we integrate automated, orchestrated systems into real work and — more importantly — how we set
      the right <strong>guardrails</strong> to keep them steering toward the goals that actually matter.
    </p>
    <p>
      This blog is where those threads come together — a space for <strong>practical lessons</strong>
      and <strong>thought experiments</strong> alike, sometimes technical, sometimes a little exotic.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="articles-section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <h2>Writings</h2>
    <div class="heading-line"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="article-filters">
    <button class="filter-btn active" data-filter="all">All</button>
    {% for cat in collections.articleCategories %}
    <button class="filter-btn" data-filter="{{ cat }}">{{ cat }}</button>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="articles-container">
    <ul class="article-list">
      {% for article in collections.articles | head(10) %}
      <li class="article-item" data-category="{{ article.data.category or 'Misc' }}">
        <h3 class="article-title">
          <a href="{{ article.url }}">{{ article.data.title }}</a>
        </h3>
        <div class="article-meta">
          <time class="article-date">{{ article.data.date | dateFormat }}</time>
          {% if article.data.category %}
          <span class="article-meta-dot">&middot;</span>
          <span class="article-category">{{ article.data.category }}</span>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        {% if article.data.description %}
        <p class="article-description">{{ article.data.description }}</p>
        {% endif %}
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>

    <div class="no-articles-message">
      <p>No articles found in this category.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  {% if collections.articles.length > 10 %}
  <p><a href="/articles/">View all articles &rarr;</a></p>
  {% endif %}
</section>
